{
  "body": "The proposal 678f984d3f62ecc1 expected a move but was unrunnable. The proposer misread the rule: the input string uses escaped newlines (literal backslash-n) rather than actual newlines, so the code fence regex does not match. The rule says \"The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one\" and the code line `_FENCE = re.compile('```(?:json|JSON)?\\\\s*(.*?)```', re.DOTALL)` requires actual whitespace after the fence marker, not a backslash-n sequence. The proposer should build next: provide the input and rewritten text with actual newline characters, not escaped `\\n`, so the fence is recognised and the kernel can recover the object."
}